{#- DeepSeek-V4 (encoding_dsv4) chat-template SENTINEL.

    memra does NOT execute jinja; it detects the dsv4 dialect by two structural markers in the
    raw template string and reproduces encoding_dsv4.py in Rust (crates/memra-tokenizer/src/
    chat.rs `apply_dsv4_template`). This file is the detection stand-in used by the
    `dsv4_template_fixtures` gate. The real DeepSeek-V4 GGUF ships a jinja that renders the
    same encoding and therefore carries the same two markers used by `template_is_dsv4()`: the
    assistant turn prefix and the DSML tool-call markup token (both appear in the body below).

    This sentinel deliberately contains NONE of the other dialects' detection substrings so
    dispatch cannot mis-route (see chat.rs / worker.rs caps for the full marker set). Do not add
    any qwen / step35 / gemma / hy3 / chatml marker text to this file, comments included: the
    caps probe and renderer dispatch are pure substring tests over the raw template.
-#}
{{ bos_token }}{%- for m in messages -%}
{%- if m.role == 'user' -%}<｜User｜>{{ m.content }}
{%- elif m.role == 'assistant' -%}<｜Assistant｜>{{ m.content }}
{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{#- tool calls use the ｜DSML｜ markup token. -#}
